<section class="section legal-content"><h2>Services</h2><p>Services are delivered according to the agreed project scope, milestones, technology and commercial terms.</p><h2>Scope & revisions</h2><p>Project scope, number of pages/screens, integrations and included revisions should be documented before development starts.</p><h2>Payments</h2><p>Replace this section with your actual deposit, milestone, invoice and payment terms.</p><h2>Client responsibilities</h2><p>The client is responsible for providing accurate content, access and approvals needed for the agreed work.</p><h2>Third-party services</h2><p>Hosting, domains, payment providers, APIs, plugins, advertising spend and other third-party costs may be separate from development fees.</p><h2>Intellectual property</h2><p>Define ownership, licensing, source-code delivery and third-party component rights in the signed agreement.</p><h2>Support</h2><p>Maintenance and support should be defined separately with response times, included hours and exclusions.</p></section>
